



⭐ 1. Plugin shape (the contract)

Each plugin is just a module that exports a simple object:

Plugin = {
  id: string,
  name: string,
  init(viewerContext),
  onFrame(frameState),
  render(ctx),
  onDestroy?()
}

id: stable identifier

name: human label

init: called once, gets viewerContext

onFrame: called every frame with current state

render: draws on its own canvas/layer

onDestroy: optional cleanup

No inheritance.No decorators.Just a plain object.

⭐ 2. Viewer context

viewerContext is the only thing plugins see:

viewerContext = {
  getFrameState(): FrameState,
  getSettings(): Settings,
  getBlueprint(): Blueprint | null,
  getViewport(): { width, height, zoom, pan },
  events: {
    on(eventName, handler),
    off(eventName, handler)
  }
}

Plugins can:

read current frame

read settings

read blueprint structure

know viewport geometry

subscribe to events like play, pause, seek, click, probe

They cannot:

change core engine behavior

mutate global state directly

⭐ 3. Plugin manager

The viewer has a tiny PluginManager:

PluginManager.load(pluginModule)
PluginManager.enable(id)
PluginManager.disable(id)
PluginManager.unload(id)
PluginManager.list()

Internally:

keeps a list of active plugins

calls init once

calls onFrame every frame

calls render in the overlay pass

calls onDestroy on unload

That’s the whole thing.

⭐ 4. Rendering model

Each plugin gets its own canvas layer:

stacked above base overlays

below HUD (or configurable)

Render order:

base media

core overlays (Θ, Ξ, organisms, metric)

plugin layers

HUD

Plugins draw only inside their own canvas.No plugin can overwrite another’s buffer.

⭐ 5. Plugin types (examples)

All plugins are the same shape—only behavior differs:

Analysis plugin

draws custom graphs, probes, annotations

Overlay plugin

adds new visual layers (e.g., custom field, debug grid)

HUD plugin

adds extra HUD panels or stats

Export plugin

listens to frames and writes logs / snapshots

No special casing in the system—just different uses of the same contract.

⭐ 6. Discovery & loading

Simplest model:

plugins live in a plugins/ folder

each plugin is one file exporting Plugin

viewer has a Plugins panel listing:

id

name

enable/disable toggle

No registry.No marketplace.Just files.



